							<p class=pText>
							The Knights of the Soyokaze are going to start a weekly lottery for the Solusek Ro server, any guild member will sell tickets, they will cost 1pp each a person can buy any number. here are the rules:<BR> <BR>
Lottery Rules: <BR>
<BR>
The Person buying the ticket will pick three(3) numbers ranging from One(1) to Ten(10), those three numbers are to be recorded by the person selling the ticket by taking a screenshot of the consumer stating the numbers they have chosen, and also using /ooc to announce to the zone what numbers they have chosen. If the consumer wishes you may use the /random function to choose the three(3) numbers for the player. 
<BR><BR>
For the Drawing of the winning numbers the Guildmaster or an Officer will use the /random command in full view of anyone who wishes to be present at the tunnel to North Ro in the East Commanlands zone, on Antonica. 
<BR><BR>
The Person or Persons that have the numbers that match the numbers drawn by the Guildmaster or Officer conducting the lottery will win 95% of all money collected. In the event that more than one person has the winning numbers those players shall split the 95% collected with all winners. The remaining 5% will be used to purchase items to use as prizes in other events we have planned. 
<BR><BR>
If no winning numbers are drawn we will carry all money earned over to the next week and build upon it, also any who purchased a ticket during a week in which a prize was not awarded will have their ticket carry over to he next week. The Lottery itself will be held every Friday night at 6:00pm PST, tickets will be sold up to a half an hour before the drawing(5:30pm PST) 
<BR><BR>
DO NOT buy a ticket from anyone that does not have a Knights of the Soyokaze guildtag on their name, and please make sure you also copy down your numbers. Winners will be notified in game, and prize money will be taken to wherever they would like to meet. For any further information please contact us at: <a href=http://members.xoom.com/solusek/event.htm>members.xoom.com/solusek/event.htm</a>. 
<BR><BR>
Thanks for your time and good luck,<BR>
Maligneto Vermagnuson, <BR>
High Officer, Knights of the Soyokaze <BR>


