						<p class="pDate">Wednesday, November 03, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">War! </p>
							<p class=pText>
							<p>
From high in the stone hallway of the Tribunal I watched the events which led up to the war.
It was firece, and the scales of balance and absolute justice were being tipped.  The Halls of The Six Hammers shook with displeasure from the Tribunal as his mighty followers whom had been slain were called to him.  I was among them.
He told us of many things, things which are sealed in my mouth as well as my mind, but this I know, we had to staop the army of the Dark ones any way we could.
I found myself in the Karanas not far from Highhold and ran unharmed to the wooden bridge which links the vast lands of East and North Karana.  Upon reaching the bridge I saw many fine warriors and clerics of Tunare.  It was very clear battle was approaching, but it never came.
People were killing off the various dark elven army in the area but none were advancing to Highhold.  Immediatly my soul was filled with fury.
I shouted at the ones who would not test the gates of Highkeep, trying to build the fire of battle in their hearts....I was successful.  While some did stay behind we ammassed a rather large force at the edge of Highhold.
After we made a plan ready, we stormed in.
It was fierce.  Four generals stormed us as we entered.  Once all our men were inside the generals fell easily enough.
Few were hesitant to found the corner as were there reported 3 elites of Innoruuk's army.
We rounded it anyway.
We found one elite and set upon him taking him down with some effort and made our way to Highkeep.
Upon entereing the gates however we found a powerful Elite among us whom was dropping our casters like flies.
The warriors and fighters quickly surrounded him as our casters backed up to cast their violent spells.
After about 1/4 our losses the Elite fell at the steps of Highkeep.
It was not over...the third, even more powerful than the last emerged.
I ran to the front lines and begin fighting as best I could, we would have lost that day had it not been for the reinforcements which came running down the halls of the castle of highkeep.
As a army we fought with an awesome might, but again, twas a mighty foe we battled and he felled 1/2 our army.
After the commotion settled, we looked around, bodies were everywhere!
Just then a shout issued! 4 elites were heading our way!!!
The call was made to retreat toward Rivervale with Carson McCabe.  I however was not allowed to go as my god saw it fit to take my soul back into the cold halls of the Six Hammers and thus from there I watched as losses were sustained on both sides, but eventually, the stinking Tier'Dal were driven back.
They had done it!!
Balance was restored!
For Now....

</p>
							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
						<p class="pDate">Tuesday, November 02, 1999</p>
						<p class="pTitle">The GM Wedding </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Hideaki server GM to Guide Tierra
<BR><BR>
The sky had shone brightly as the sun began its set upon the far shores, 
dissappearing over the lake. The Priestess of Erollisi Marr had appeared upon 
the docs with her long raven tresses cascading off of her flowing scarlet 
robes. Before her stood Lord Hideaki Tendo, the Avatar of Erollisi Marr with 
his bethrothed, Tierra The Loved. Behind them stood Lady Skyestorm alongside 
Lord Tiganos, both respectively best man and maid of honor. Also present twas 
Sir Banegrivm as the bearer of rings.
<BR><BR>
The party stood upon oaken docs that carried out upon the waters with the 
processional to entowned. All the masses from far and wide, both of light and 
of dark twere gatherd in full regalia for the occasion at hand. Hideaki's 
armor glinted brilliantly within the setting sun as the two exchanged vows 
that day. The Avatar of Erollisi twas as that legendary figure that had 
emerged from tales of old of white knights in gleaming plate who would ride 
upon white steads to save a fair maiden in distress. He held the hand of his 
love who gazed at him longingly, her eyes aglow like the most beautiful of 
Kaladims saphires.
<BR><BR>
Tierra The Loved stood with her tresses kept beneath the veil of purity in 
state. Her matching gown flowed downwards to the ground sweepingly with every 
flouring movement. This had been a day she had long awaited. Until this very 
moment she had never known of her past that brought her departure from Neriak 
and her mark of Erollisi upon her that fated her from her birthright. Nor had 
she known her name which translated Teir'Ra meant elven love. All this came 
to memory with but a white mist that billowed forth from the priestess 
revealing her past.
<BR><BR>
Hideaki took his loves hand as the vows continued onwards. Both lost within 
the depths of Erollisi's gift upon them for upon this day they were two fated 
from destiny onwards. The vows ended as the rings were placed upon fingers. 
The priestess smiles as she spoke her final words "I know pronounce you 
husband and wife, you may kiss the bride". Nervously the Avatar of Love drew 
his brides veil from her face and embraced her in a kiss that spoke a 
thousand words.
<BR><BR>
It was upon this day many stood to give honor to two who often walked the 
lands to aid those without a simple thanks. A time when many came to honor 
true love in its most pure and holy form. This would be a time that would 
embark upon beginning glories in Norrath. A time when one house would stand 
united in Norrath in the pursuits of the gods upon high...enter the House of 
Tendo, for upon that day Hideaki and Tierra would remain as one...ascent into 
hereafter.
<BR> <BR>

my gift to the wedded:<BR>
<BR>
"the Call of Love"<BR>
<BR>
Tis spake once upon a merried moon,<BR>
 hence mine lost love borne.<BR>
I prayed for all but mercy,<BR>
 unto the coming o' that morn.<BR>
I watched her gentle mercy,<BR>
 each time she draweth near.<BR>
Therein her sight I felt her touch,<BR>
 and cried out yet none didst hear.<BR>
Upon the field she sat and watched the rose,<BR>
 as it breathed life into its bloom.<BR>
She picted his embrace of love,<BR>
 whence she befell his gallant grace.<BR>
Bestowed twas she to such tender mercies,<BR>
 whence his arm did take past tears.<BR>
For upon one fatefull eve <BR>those prayers came true,<BR>
 the call of love,<BR>
  sweet bliss didst come endeared.<BR>
<BR><BR>
Author - Sir Banegrivm <BR>Blackheart

							<br>
							 - Aanamdar<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
